1
00:01:02,535 --> 00:01:03,655
[Beast: Answer me]

2
00:01:05,215 --> 00:01:08,153
What's going on?

3
00:01:48,808 --> 00:01:51,415
That unhinged bastard!

4
00:01:54,855 --> 00:01:56,121
[Beast]
Just hold on.

5
00:01:56,121 --> 00:01:58,881
I'm going home right now
to smash the camcorder.

6
00:01:58,881 --> 00:02:00,581
Camcorder?

7
00:02:14,475 --> 00:02:17,327
If we smash the camcorder now
and flee to the future...

8
00:02:17,988 --> 00:02:22,771
it still won't change the fact that
Yoon Ha Na got kidnapped here, in the past!

9
00:02:24,095 --> 00:02:26,072
I'm the only one who can save her...

10
00:02:26,072 --> 00:02:27,772
right now.

11
00:02:52,501 --> 00:02:54,426
What... is this?

12
00:02:57,095 --> 00:02:59,945
Year... 2026?

13
00:03:04,728 --> 00:03:07,192
I'm just curious.

14
00:03:07,192 --> 00:03:09,509
Why would you quit acting?

15
00:03:09,509 --> 00:03:11,066
Jun Mo...

16
00:03:11,066 --> 00:03:12,766
Why!

17
00:03:16,572 --> 00:03:18,423
I'm asking you.

18
00:03:20,993 --> 00:03:24,294
What, in the future you just came back from...

19
00:03:25,497 --> 00:03:27,812
Did I kill you or something?

20
00:03:35,821 --> 00:03:37,521
Jun Mo, I...

21
00:03:38,521 --> 00:03:42,025
I don't think you're making much sense.

22
00:03:43,601 --> 00:03:45,905
Do you really think it's so improbable?

23
00:03:49,448 --> 00:03:51,621
I think it does make sense.

24
00:03:51,621 --> 00:03:53,822
In fact, I'm pretty sure of it.

25
00:03:54,801 --> 00:03:57,993
- Jun Mo...
- Don't beat around the bush, just tell me.

26
00:03:59,128 --> 00:04:00,828
Ha Na!

27
00:04:19,635 --> 00:04:22,020
I'm sorry, Ha Na. Are you alright?

28
00:04:24,921 --> 00:04:27,695
I-I wasn't in my right mind.

29
00:04:28,461 --> 00:04:29,940
Are you okay?

30
00:04:39,888 --> 00:04:42,874
Yang Jun Mo, you bastard, where are you?

31
00:04:47,928 --> 00:04:49,425
Hello?

32
00:04:50,295 --> 00:04:51,995
Yeah, come quickly.

33
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:57,269
[Episode 10]

34
00:05:04,648 --> 00:05:06,348
I'm sorry, Ha Na.

35
00:05:08,495 --> 00:05:11,225
I just wanted to convince you with my synopsis,

36
00:05:11,225 --> 00:05:12,925
but I flew off the handle.

37
00:05:14,521 --> 00:05:16,221
The script...

38
00:05:16,841 --> 00:05:18,541
What is it?

39
00:05:19,535 --> 00:05:20,901
It's a temporary title for now,

40
00:05:20,901 --> 00:05:23,385
but it's called "Lost Time."

41
00:05:23,385 --> 00:05:25,109
"Lost time?"

42
00:05:25,109 --> 00:05:27,860
It's about using an old camcorder
to travel back and forth in time.

43
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:32,676
I was stuck on giving the female protagonist
a compelling motive to travel back in time,

44
00:05:32,676 --> 00:05:35,016
but talking with you gave me
a spark of an idea.

45
00:05:35,635 --> 00:05:38,434
What if the protagonist died?

46
00:05:38,434 --> 00:05:42,851
For the protagonist to have
a strong motivation to travel back in time,

47
00:05:42,851 --> 00:05:45,202
someone would have to die.

48
00:05:45,202 --> 00:05:46,679
That's the idea.

49
00:05:46,679 --> 00:05:49,503
The scenario is supposed to be written in 2026.

50
00:05:49,503 --> 00:05:52,627
Did my rejection cause it to be written sooner?

51
00:05:52,627 --> 00:05:54,327
I've been thinking of you, and only you...

52
00:05:56,148 --> 00:05:57,352
What?

53
00:05:57,352 --> 00:05:59,756
the whole time I was writing the script.

54
00:05:59,756 --> 00:06:01,960
We've been doing so well up until now,

55
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:05,185
and I've never doubted our future
for even a second.

56
00:06:06,997 --> 00:06:08,968
I'm sorry, Jun Mo.

57
00:06:08,968 --> 00:06:10,254
Ha Na.

58
00:06:11,237 --> 00:06:13,717
I mean it with all my heart when I say this.

59
00:06:13,717 --> 00:06:15,488
I hope you don't give up on acting.

60
00:06:15,488 --> 00:06:17,232
You don't have to do my movie.

61
00:06:17,232 --> 00:06:19,269
Please, just reconsider it.

62
00:06:19,269 --> 00:06:21,520
Just think about whether you, Ha Na,

63
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:24,571
will be able to live a happy life
as anything other than an actress.

64
00:06:27,277 --> 00:06:29,277
You are...

65
00:06:29,277 --> 00:06:30,977
the best actress ever, at least to me.

66
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:33,424
Whatever anyone else says,

67
00:06:33,424 --> 00:06:35,561
you are the best ever, at least in my life.

68
00:06:36,313 --> 00:06:37,607
Got it?

69
00:06:46,724 --> 00:06:48,149
Ha Na!

70
00:06:49,190 --> 00:06:51,263
You bastard!

71
00:06:54,042 --> 00:06:55,494
Let's go.

72
00:07:20,984 --> 00:07:23,160
Are you sure you're okay?

73
00:07:24,194 --> 00:07:26,196
Yeah, I'm fine.

74
00:07:26,196 --> 00:07:29,191
What can I do to get back to that lunatic?

75
00:07:31,410 --> 00:07:33,066
Desperation.

76
00:07:33,704 --> 00:07:36,334
Yang Jun Mo's heart was filled with it.

77
00:07:36,334 --> 00:07:38,584
What are you going on about now?

78
00:07:38,584 --> 00:07:40,680
He was just so desperate...

79
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:44,102
to be good at something.

80
00:07:45,910 --> 00:07:48,004
Desperation? Wanting to be good at something?

81
00:07:48,004 --> 00:07:49,988
That's not an excuse for his behavior!

82
00:07:51,717 --> 00:07:53,710
What he did is just wrong.

83
00:07:53,710 --> 00:07:56,944
Don't let pity or sympathy
get the better of you.

84
00:07:56,944 --> 00:07:58,228
Yoon Ha Na.

85
00:07:58,228 --> 00:08:00,140
Pity should be reserved for human beings.

86
00:08:00,804 --> 00:08:03,377
Don't waste it on those lesser than human.

87
00:08:06,069 --> 00:08:08,444
Can't Jun Mo's future...

88
00:08:09,157 --> 00:08:11,514
change, as Hyeong Won's did?

89
00:08:11,514 --> 00:08:13,034
Yoon Ha Na.

90
00:08:14,944 --> 00:08:18,381
We are, in fact, somehow
traveling through time right now,

91
00:08:18,381 --> 00:08:20,317
but we're not gods.

92
00:08:23,477 --> 00:08:25,637
We...

93
00:08:25,637 --> 00:08:28,475
should just stick to doing our best
at what we can manage.

94
00:08:30,910 --> 00:08:32,286
Okay.

95
00:08:41,704 --> 00:08:44,901
First of all, Lee Hyeong Won is
on the semi-pro judo team now,

96
00:08:44,901 --> 00:08:47,825
so it wouldn't make sense for him to
team up with Jun Mo to come for you.

97
00:08:47,825 --> 00:08:52,073
Does someone else take up
Lee Hyeong Won's role in the narrative, then?

98
00:08:52,073 --> 00:08:54,504
Or maybe it just doesn't happen at all.

99
00:08:55,619 --> 00:08:57,504
I wish that was the case.

100
00:08:57,504 --> 00:09:00,034
Yang Jun Mo is the stalker...

101
00:09:00,034 --> 00:09:02,558
Then what's the deal with Lee Hyeong Won?

102
00:09:02,558 --> 00:09:04,382
What do they have to do with each other?

103
00:09:04,382 --> 00:09:08,173
Besides, didn't he originally disappear
during sophomore year?

104
00:09:08,173 --> 00:09:11,484
- What could this mean?
- Why would they gang up on not only you,

105
00:09:11,484 --> 00:09:14,035
but Woo Jae as well? There's no reason to!

106
00:09:14,717 --> 00:09:16,795
I have no clue.

107
00:09:18,984 --> 00:09:21,224
Should we just go after Lee Hyeong Won first?

108
00:09:21,224 --> 00:09:24,604
Apparently, he's best friends with Woo Jae,
so you should approach him and...

109
00:09:26,990 --> 00:09:28,690
Where have you been?

110
00:09:30,550 --> 00:09:33,015
- Woo Jae.
- Hey, what are you...

111
00:09:33,015 --> 00:09:34,978
What were you doing here?

112
00:09:34,978 --> 00:09:36,942
Ha Na wasn't picking up my calls.

113
00:09:36,942 --> 00:09:40,752
My schedule got canceled,
so I came by to see you, Ha Na.

114
00:09:41,786 --> 00:09:44,644
I lost my phone.

115
00:09:44,644 --> 00:09:46,684
What happened? Should we go get a new one?

116
00:09:46,684 --> 00:09:49,185
No, no. I want to look for it a bit more.

117
00:09:51,230 --> 00:09:53,716
I was thinking we could
go on a date near the Han River.

118
00:09:55,484 --> 00:09:57,264
Sure.

119
00:09:57,264 --> 00:10:00,104
I'm going to the convenience store.
Do you want anything?

120
00:10:00,104 --> 00:10:01,488
- Nope.
- No, thank you.

121
00:10:01,488 --> 00:10:02,762
I'll be quick.

122
00:10:44,224 --> 00:10:46,250
Concentrate on the movie.

123
00:10:46,957 --> 00:10:48,574
I know, but...

124
00:10:48,574 --> 00:10:50,218
You're just so pretty.

125
00:10:50,218 --> 00:10:52,543
I can't concentrate at all.

126
00:10:54,037 --> 00:10:55,737
Stop being silly.

127
00:11:03,038 --> 00:11:04,277
My...

128
00:11:04,896 --> 00:11:06,274
Saving...

129
00:11:06,274 --> 00:11:09,317
"Saving you in my heart!"

130
00:11:09,317 --> 00:11:12,210
What on earth did I just witness?

131
00:11:13,224 --> 00:11:14,908
You don't know this?

132
00:11:14,908 --> 00:11:16,904
It's a trend that's going on.

133
00:11:16,904 --> 00:11:19,929
"Saving you in my heart!"

134
00:11:24,188 --> 00:11:26,654
That's weird. He said you'd love this.

135
00:11:26,654 --> 00:11:29,056
- Who told you that?
- Soo Hyuk.

136
00:11:30,148 --> 00:11:31,205
Was it a prank?

137
00:11:31,205 --> 00:11:33,480
I'm going to give him a piece of my mind.

138
00:11:34,374 --> 00:11:37,276
"Saving you in my heart!"

139
00:11:37,914 --> 00:11:40,681
- Stop that.
- "Saving!"

140
00:11:40,681 --> 00:11:42,381
You're adorable.

141
00:11:46,957 --> 00:11:48,348
I'm sorry.

142
00:11:48,348 --> 00:11:51,741
Sorry that we can't leave the car,
let alone go to the movies.

143
00:11:51,741 --> 00:11:53,166
Whatever.

144
00:11:53,166 --> 00:11:57,174
I prefer being alone with you
over being in a crowded movie theater.

145
00:11:57,174 --> 00:11:59,714
See? We can hold hands, judgment-free!

146
00:11:59,714 --> 00:12:01,414
I absolutely love it.

147
00:12:02,314 --> 00:12:03,787
Thank you.

148
00:12:06,852 --> 00:12:08,445
Woo Jae.

149
00:12:08,445 --> 00:12:09,782
Yes?

150
00:12:09,782 --> 00:12:11,482
You know, I...

151
00:12:12,968 --> 00:12:16,208
I hope you live a happy life, Woo Jae.

152
00:12:16,208 --> 00:12:18,708
And a long one at that.

153
00:12:20,534 --> 00:12:23,978
Well, I am really happy right now.

154
00:12:25,829 --> 00:12:27,279
Me too.

155
00:12:34,561 --> 00:12:35,997
Woo Jae.

156
00:12:37,268 --> 00:12:39,221
If...

157
00:12:39,221 --> 00:12:41,468
Hypothetically speaking...

158
00:12:43,734 --> 00:12:47,132
Imagine we broke up in a really bad way.

159
00:12:50,768 --> 00:12:53,170
I don't see that happening, but...

160
00:12:53,828 --> 00:12:55,370
Okay, if so, then what?

161
00:12:56,454 --> 00:12:58,154
I will...

162
00:12:59,614 --> 00:13:02,064
wish you happiness with all my heart

163
00:13:02,699 --> 00:13:04,955
wherever you end up without me,

164
00:13:05,561 --> 00:13:08,468
and whoever you end up with.
Even if it isn't me.

165
00:13:11,768 --> 00:13:13,468
For me...

166
00:13:15,228 --> 00:13:18,817
the fact that I can love you
with everything I have...

167
00:13:19,808 --> 00:13:21,663
just gives me so much joy.

168
00:13:23,074 --> 00:13:25,040
It makes me happy.

169
00:13:30,154 --> 00:13:33,023
Ha Na. I need to ask you this.

170
00:13:34,082 --> 00:13:36,718
Did you refuse to star
in Director Yang Jun Mo's film...

171
00:13:36,718 --> 00:13:38,831
because of me?

172
00:13:38,831 --> 00:13:40,655
Because I didn't want you to?

173
00:13:40,655 --> 00:13:44,505
The script wasn't all made up.

174
00:13:46,551 --> 00:13:50,423
No, I just made a decision
after thinking long and hard about it.

175
00:13:52,871 --> 00:13:54,248
Woo Jae.

176
00:13:54,248 --> 00:13:56,526
Could you tell me...

177
00:13:56,526 --> 00:14:00,485
why you hate Jun Mo so much?

178
00:14:03,458 --> 00:14:06,208
- That's...
- I'm just curious.

179
00:14:11,264 --> 00:14:13,268
Truth be told,

180
00:14:13,268 --> 00:14:16,390
I saw something strange.

181
00:14:33,925 --> 00:14:36,384
"My little canary...

182
00:14:36,384 --> 00:14:38,097
who stole my soul?"

183
00:14:40,044 --> 00:14:41,898
"Slit its throat..."

184
00:14:42,822 --> 00:14:45,724
[My sweetheart shines brightly on the monitor.
Should I behead you and hold a funeral?]

185
00:14:45,724 --> 00:14:46,988
"My sweetheart, on the monitor..."

186
00:14:46,988 --> 00:14:48,672
Get the ones out in the front, first.

187
00:14:48,672 --> 00:14:50,383
- Yes, sir.
- Good, good.

188
00:14:53,302 --> 00:14:54,308
[50th class, Yang Jun Mo]

189
00:14:55,398 --> 00:14:58,518
The sweetheart on Jun Mo's monitor would be...

190
00:14:59,604 --> 00:15:01,304
What's up, Woo Jae?

191
00:15:11,358 --> 00:15:12,829
Woo Jae.

192
00:15:14,124 --> 00:15:16,369
Stay in your lane.

193
00:15:20,851 --> 00:15:23,978
It dropped out of the bag I was trying to pack.

194
00:15:28,064 --> 00:15:30,582
It's a little bit embarrassing, you know.

195
00:15:30,582 --> 00:15:34,219
I just scribble down
whatever idea comes to mind.

196
00:15:34,219 --> 00:15:36,976
A lot of these end up in parts of my scenarios,

197
00:15:36,976 --> 00:15:39,701
so I hope you understand
that I can't help but be secretive about it.

198
00:15:40,824 --> 00:15:42,524
Yes.

199
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:44,181
Jun Mo!

200
00:15:44,181 --> 00:15:46,098
- Are you coming?
- Yeah.

201
00:15:47,938 --> 00:15:50,653
- I have to go. See you later.
- Sure.

202
00:16:02,091 --> 00:16:03,791
Hey, Soo Hyuk!

203
00:16:07,871 --> 00:16:10,208
- Here, the pillows you asked for!
- Thank you.

204
00:16:10,208 --> 00:16:12,851
- Here you go!
- Thank you!

205
00:16:12,851 --> 00:16:14,275
We'll get going now.

206
00:16:14,275 --> 00:16:16,757
- Yeah, good job today!
- Good night.

207
00:16:17,451 --> 00:16:20,455
Director Yang, you can sleep in my room.
It's pretty crowded out here.

208
00:16:20,455 --> 00:16:21,979
Thank you.

209
00:16:21,979 --> 00:16:23,679
Hey, hey, Ha Ru!

210
00:16:25,551 --> 00:16:27,630
Our day is far from over.

211
00:16:28,254 --> 00:16:31,658
We need to talk about the correlation
between world-building and range.

212
00:16:31,658 --> 00:16:34,339
- Over there, I assume?
- I thought we just did that!

213
00:16:34,339 --> 00:16:36,058
But I already understood everything...

214
00:16:36,058 --> 00:16:38,159
There he goes again...

215
00:16:41,677 --> 00:16:43,378
Ye Rang, aren't you going to sleep?

216
00:16:43,378 --> 00:16:46,001
I just need to wrap up. You go to bed first.

217
00:16:49,317 --> 00:16:50,896
Good night!

218
00:17:09,844 --> 00:17:13,446
Stop loitering behind my back
and say what you want to say.

219
00:17:16,703 --> 00:17:18,574
Do you know...

220
00:17:18,574 --> 00:17:22,626
when Ha Na started working on
Director Jun Mo's film?

221
00:17:22,626 --> 00:17:25,196
June 5th, 2012.

222
00:17:26,904 --> 00:17:31,370
No need to be surprised.
It's just a day I'll never forget.

223
00:17:31,370 --> 00:17:35,790
That was the day of the first audition
that Ha Na took for Jun Mo's films.

224
00:17:35,790 --> 00:17:38,481
Ha Na ended up being the female lead,

225
00:17:38,481 --> 00:17:40,985
and signaled the start of
Seo Ye Rang's inability to secure a lead role.

226
00:17:40,985 --> 00:17:43,190
That's June 5th, 2012.

227
00:17:43,885 --> 00:17:46,056
So, why are you asking?

228
00:17:47,925 --> 00:17:49,432
It's nothing.

229
00:17:55,352 --> 00:17:57,725
[My little canary, who stole my soul.
You are what completes me.]

230
00:18:12,852 --> 00:18:14,427
Hey, Yoon Ha Na...

231
00:18:16,585 --> 00:18:18,285
What a sight.

232
00:18:20,492 --> 00:18:22,425
- What are they doing?
- Look at those lovebirds!

233
00:18:24,872 --> 00:18:27,076
- Let's go. Move!
- Move, move!

234
00:18:30,359 --> 00:18:31,739
Let's go!

235
00:18:32,525 --> 00:18:34,225
Yeah, let's go.

236
00:18:35,778 --> 00:18:38,016
Once I saw it,

237
00:18:38,016 --> 00:18:40,272
I couldn't stop noticing it.

238
00:18:40,272 --> 00:18:43,818
He'd get this beady look in his eyes
every time he saw you, Ha Na.

239
00:18:44,425 --> 00:18:47,752
What, in the future you just came back from...

240
00:18:48,782 --> 00:18:50,839
Did I kill you or something?

241
00:18:50,839 --> 00:18:53,412
I'm sorry, Ha Na. Are you alright?

242
00:18:56,035 --> 00:18:58,652
I-I wasn't in my right mind.

243
00:18:59,328 --> 00:19:01,819
So, Woo Jae was the first to witness...

244
00:19:01,819 --> 00:19:03,956
Jun Mo's true face.

245
00:19:03,956 --> 00:19:05,780
Ha Na.

246
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:07,584
Do you think...

247
00:19:07,584 --> 00:19:11,548
I've become that type of guy who gets jealous
and ruins his talented girlfriend's future?

248
00:19:11,548 --> 00:19:13,825
Is that who I am now?

249
00:19:14,575 --> 00:19:16,566
No, you're not.

250
00:19:16,566 --> 00:19:22,224
Your talented girlfriend doesn't need Jun Mo
to have a good future.

251
00:19:22,224 --> 00:19:23,924
So stop worrying.

252
00:19:57,794 --> 00:19:59,310
Woo Jae.

253
00:20:00,621 --> 00:20:02,612
You know, I...

254
00:20:02,612 --> 00:20:05,461
I hope you live a happy life, Woo Jae.

255
00:20:06,281 --> 00:20:09,096
And a long one at that.

256
00:20:12,914 --> 00:20:15,636
Ha Na. I need to ask you this.

257
00:20:16,853 --> 00:20:19,532
Did you refuse to star
in Director Yang Jun Mo's film...

258
00:20:20,654 --> 00:20:22,354
because of me?

259
00:20:23,194 --> 00:20:24,899
Because I didn't want you to?

260
00:20:41,138 --> 00:20:43,568
You know I'm good friends with Reporter Yang.

261
00:20:43,568 --> 00:20:48,311
I got a tip that some journalists from ThisTrue
will be raking through the whole Han River.

262
00:20:48,311 --> 00:20:50,732
So I came running right away.

263
00:20:51,411 --> 00:20:55,808
How's this? "Ye Rang Entertainment's employees
gather for a bonding meeting at the Han River."

264
00:20:55,808 --> 00:20:59,244
We're sorry to inconvenience you, Ye Rang.

265
00:20:59,244 --> 00:21:00,882
Thank you, Ye Rang.

266
00:21:00,882 --> 00:21:03,839
No need. I'm glad to be here.

267
00:21:03,839 --> 00:21:06,210
I'm on a date, too, so...

268
00:21:06,210 --> 00:21:10,166
I haven't seen him in a while, you know.

269
00:21:13,431 --> 00:21:14,762
Really?

270
00:21:14,762 --> 00:21:17,320
I... don't recall.

271
00:21:29,424 --> 00:21:31,474
- Stop stuffing your face.
- You can have it.

272
00:22:19,378 --> 00:22:21,410
Copycat!

273
00:22:34,844 --> 00:22:39,195
I need to tell her that I'm quitting.

274
00:22:46,364 --> 00:22:49,015
Is everything okay, Ye Rang?

275
00:22:49,015 --> 00:22:50,164
Huh?

276
00:22:54,224 --> 00:22:55,631
Well...

277
00:22:56,844 --> 00:22:59,415
This isn't about me,

278
00:22:59,415 --> 00:23:02,355
but a friend of a friend of mine...

279
00:23:04,064 --> 00:23:06,332
A friend of a friend, you say?

280
00:23:07,438 --> 00:23:08,462
What is it?

281
00:23:08,462 --> 00:23:09,921
[The Hannam, Chef Mun]

282
00:23:22,898 --> 00:23:26,135
Hey, by the way, is Ha Na okay?

283
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:31,180
- What do you mean?
- She turned Director Yang Jun Mo down, right?

284
00:23:31,864 --> 00:23:34,198
Don't even mention that lunatic, Yang Jun Mo!

285
00:23:34,198 --> 00:23:37,111
He went all "Fast & Furious"
with Ha Na, and I had to...

286
00:23:37,111 --> 00:23:38,795
What did you just say?

287
00:23:38,795 --> 00:23:41,148
Yang Jun Mo did what with Ha Na?

288
00:23:43,031 --> 00:23:44,577
I mean...

289
00:23:45,551 --> 00:23:47,991
Her boyfriend is too busy.

290
00:23:49,144 --> 00:23:51,513
She waited, and waited...

291
00:23:53,064 --> 00:23:54,989
until she grew tired of waiting.

292
00:23:56,578 --> 00:23:59,389
She feels like her love is one-sided.

293
00:24:02,711 --> 00:24:04,435
She's sad and lonely.

294
00:24:04,435 --> 00:24:05,688
Very.

295
00:24:07,363 --> 00:24:09,298
Sounds like a joke of a boyfriend.

296
00:24:09,298 --> 00:24:12,108
Who does he think he is,
making his girlfriend feel lonely?

297
00:24:18,531 --> 00:24:22,096
If they're letting the present slip away
because of the future...

298
00:24:23,171 --> 00:24:25,289
it's not really love, is it?

299
00:24:27,944 --> 00:24:31,680
So, Yang Jun Mo did that, huh?

300
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:32,958
Yeah.

301
00:24:32,958 --> 00:24:36,691
Yoon Ha Na told me not to tell you
because you'd get worried, but...

302
00:24:38,103 --> 00:24:40,048
I'll pretend I didn't hear that. But...

303
00:24:40,048 --> 00:24:43,051
you need to tell me
if anything happens to Ha Na.

304
00:24:43,051 --> 00:24:45,324
Yeah, of course!

305
00:25:03,171 --> 00:25:05,655
- Are you alright?
- Me?

306
00:25:05,655 --> 00:25:07,038
What about me?

307
00:25:07,038 --> 00:25:09,528
- Are you dense?
- Why?

308
00:25:09,528 --> 00:25:11,875
Am... I dense?

309
00:25:12,798 --> 00:25:16,285
When's the last time you and Ye Rang
went on a proper date?

310
00:25:18,518 --> 00:25:20,238
I'm not sure.

311
00:25:20,238 --> 00:25:23,691
I guess Yoon Ha Ru isn't just dense,
but a lost cause as well.

312
00:25:23,691 --> 00:25:25,798
What do you mean by that?

313
00:25:25,798 --> 00:25:29,318
Don't let your cherished one get away.

314
00:25:29,318 --> 00:25:31,268
I'm not exactly planning to.

315
00:25:31,268 --> 00:25:32,804
When you're blinded by purpose,

316
00:25:32,804 --> 00:25:35,849
you might lose sight of what really matters.

317
00:25:36,471 --> 00:25:38,922
I can see my cherished one clear as day!

318
00:25:38,922 --> 00:25:40,699
- Crystal clear!
- Okay.

319
00:25:40,699 --> 00:25:42,651
Good for you.

320
00:25:42,651 --> 00:25:44,892
- Let's go.
- Aren't you playing?

321
00:25:45,484 --> 00:25:47,804
- Come on, one more round!
- I said no.

322
00:25:47,804 --> 00:25:50,237
- Scared of losing?
- I'm not playing.

323
00:25:58,004 --> 00:25:59,802
- Are you done playing?
- Yeah.

324
00:25:59,802 --> 00:26:02,162
- I won!
- Really?

325
00:27:47,944 --> 00:27:50,835
- Who is it?
- Delivery for Yoon Ha Na.

326
00:27:50,835 --> 00:27:53,416
What? One minute!

327
00:28:01,398 --> 00:28:03,864
- I'm going out.
- Okay.

328
00:28:03,864 --> 00:28:06,340
- You're going out, too?
- I've got a delivery.

329
00:28:15,936 --> 00:28:18,097
Nothing to do...

330
00:28:20,591 --> 00:28:21,438
[Jung Woo Jae]

331
00:28:25,330 --> 00:28:27,749
Yes, it's me. Are you bored?

332
00:28:27,749 --> 00:28:30,003
What? No, I'm on the set.

333
00:28:32,004 --> 00:28:33,046
What is it?

334
00:28:33,046 --> 00:28:35,252
I might be a little paranoid,

335
00:28:35,252 --> 00:28:37,436
but could you go to the shared house for me?

336
00:28:37,436 --> 00:28:39,303
Isn't Yoon Ha Na there?

337
00:28:39,303 --> 00:28:41,799
Why? Is something wrong?

338
00:28:41,799 --> 00:28:43,888
Not particularly.

339
00:28:43,888 --> 00:28:46,042
Come on, help me out.

340
00:28:47,004 --> 00:28:49,908
But it's my three days off.

341
00:28:49,908 --> 00:28:52,846
Is it really a good idea to make me protect
my best friend's girlfriend

342
00:28:52,846 --> 00:28:55,176
who also happens to be my first love,
who so brutally turned me down?

343
00:28:56,804 --> 00:28:58,695
I did an advertisement for Ike yesterday.

344
00:28:58,695 --> 00:29:00,992
They gifted me a... what was it again?

345
00:29:00,992 --> 00:29:03,096
An off-black Ike Jordan?

346
00:29:03,096 --> 00:29:04,947
- What the hell?
- It's a limited edition,

347
00:29:04,947 --> 00:29:06,604
so money can't buy it, or so I've heard.

348
00:29:06,604 --> 00:29:09,084
- What size?
- 285.

349
00:29:09,084 --> 00:29:10,314
Deal?

350
00:29:11,835 --> 00:29:14,433
Deal. You sly bastard.

351
00:29:27,858 --> 00:29:30,230
What's this? Do you think Woo Jae sent this?

352
00:29:30,230 --> 00:29:31,930
Is this some kind of surprise?

353
00:29:43,450 --> 00:29:45,599
Which sick bastard did this?

354
00:29:50,951 --> 00:29:52,258
Hey...

355
00:29:56,014 --> 00:29:57,586
You there!

356
00:30:09,468 --> 00:30:10,935
Hey.

357
00:30:13,908 --> 00:30:15,608
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru!

358
00:30:18,527 --> 00:30:20,175
Are you okay?

359
00:30:20,946 --> 00:30:22,294
Wait here.

360
00:30:28,368 --> 00:30:29,817
Hey, Lee Hyeong Won!

361
00:30:29,817 --> 00:30:31,458
Get that bastard!

362
00:30:31,458 --> 00:30:32,841
Who?

363
00:30:44,188 --> 00:30:45,888
You maniac!

364
00:30:53,154 --> 00:30:55,884
Good to see you again, Lee Hyeong Won.

365
00:31:16,428 --> 00:31:18,128
Hey, Lee Hyeong Won!

366
00:31:23,494 --> 00:31:25,397
Hello, emergency services?

367
00:31:26,040 --> 00:31:28,216
Someone's been injured!

368
00:31:53,208 --> 00:31:54,992
They said that,
with proper treatment and rehabilitation,

369
00:31:54,992 --> 00:31:57,628
he'll recover by the end of the year.

370
00:31:57,628 --> 00:32:01,194
He'll be okay. He has Woo Jae with him,

371
00:32:01,194 --> 00:32:03,310
and his team will take care of him.

372
00:32:06,581 --> 00:32:09,081
That would've originally been Lee Hyeong Won,

373
00:32:09,081 --> 00:32:11,508
but someone else
took his place in the narrative.

374
00:32:11,508 --> 00:32:15,127
Lee Hyeong Won, on the other hand,
got injured because of us.

375
00:32:18,438 --> 00:32:20,148
Jun Mo...

376
00:32:20,148 --> 00:32:22,334
If I hadn't turned his movie pitch down,

377
00:32:22,334 --> 00:32:26,141
he would've still been
a good mentor, and a good director.

378
00:32:26,141 --> 00:32:27,954
It's because I turned him down.

379
00:32:27,954 --> 00:32:30,714
I made him reveal his true colors sooner.

380
00:32:30,714 --> 00:32:32,202
No.

381
00:32:32,202 --> 00:32:35,464
He's always been a horrible guy.
It just came to light faster than before.

382
00:32:36,582 --> 00:32:39,227
The fragments of the past
that we twisted have stacked up

383
00:32:39,227 --> 00:32:42,217
and introduced too many
unpredictable variables.

384
00:32:42,217 --> 00:32:44,705
Someone even got hurt.

385
00:32:47,034 --> 00:32:49,592
Get it together, Yoon Ha Na.

386
00:32:49,592 --> 00:32:52,389
Yes, things have gone wrong,
and yes, there are more variables,

387
00:32:52,389 --> 00:32:54,649
but everything that should happen has happened.

388
00:32:55,561 --> 00:32:56,676
Everything that should happen?

389
00:32:56,676 --> 00:32:57,961
You can't even cry!

390
00:32:57,961 --> 00:33:00,045
The unrelenting stalking...

391
00:33:00,934 --> 00:33:02,943
has started, just like it should.

392
00:33:05,527 --> 00:33:08,432
I am sorry about Lee Hyeong Won.

393
00:33:08,432 --> 00:33:10,502
But this variable is giving us an advantage.

394
00:33:10,502 --> 00:33:12,940
He even went ahead and made a mistake!

395
00:33:12,940 --> 00:33:15,784
Every trace that Yang Jun Mo
leaves behind from now on

396
00:33:15,784 --> 00:33:17,790
is all proof that we can use.

397
00:33:21,457 --> 00:33:25,039
He'll... show up again soon, right?

398
00:33:25,039 --> 00:33:27,389
We need to prove that Yang Jun Mo is a stalker,

399
00:33:27,389 --> 00:33:29,840
and that he hurt someone.

400
00:33:29,840 --> 00:33:32,105
It's the only way we'll lock him away for good.

401
00:33:33,037 --> 00:33:36,614
Time is on our side now.

402
00:33:41,337 --> 00:33:42,829
Lee Hyeong Won...

403
00:33:50,057 --> 00:33:51,632
What?

404
00:33:52,504 --> 00:33:55,517
So what you're saying is,
the bastard who did this to you

405
00:33:55,517 --> 00:33:58,045
is someone you know?

406
00:34:00,204 --> 00:34:02,435
Who is it? Where does he live?

407
00:34:02,435 --> 00:34:04,987
I should go find this bastard and...

408
00:34:14,771 --> 00:34:16,471
Who is it?

409
00:34:18,604 --> 00:34:20,304
Park Gi Tae.

410
00:34:21,311 --> 00:34:23,297
Park Gi Tae?

411
00:34:23,297 --> 00:34:26,515
Thank you for lending me your precious time.

412
00:34:26,515 --> 00:34:30,771
This here is Jung Woo Jae's updated profile.

413
00:34:30,771 --> 00:34:33,461
- He's very handsome.
- What a good-looking guy.

414
00:34:33,461 --> 00:34:35,225
He's perfect for our newest project.

415
00:34:35,225 --> 00:34:36,751
It seems that way.

416
00:34:36,751 --> 00:34:40,847
And this is Yoon Ha Na's profile.

417
00:34:44,209 --> 00:34:46,681
You know I'm
a collector of great actors, right?

418
00:34:46,681 --> 00:34:48,685
We know Yoon Ha Na, of course.

419
00:34:48,685 --> 00:34:50,903
I enjoyed "The Masked Season."

420
00:34:50,903 --> 00:34:54,261
Writer Geum, you must be so busy.
How did you find the time to watch it?

421
00:34:54,261 --> 00:34:57,477
It's Jeon Hee Ae's work. How could I miss it?

422
00:34:59,711 --> 00:35:01,691
Right, of course.

423
00:35:02,297 --> 00:35:03,915
CEO Seo.

424
00:35:03,915 --> 00:35:05,195
Yes, Ms. Geum?

425
00:35:05,195 --> 00:35:08,439
I'll be honest, since it's you.

426
00:35:08,439 --> 00:35:12,163
Our new project needs a female lead
that's globally recognized.

427
00:35:12,163 --> 00:35:14,342
I'm sure you understand.

428
00:35:15,675 --> 00:35:17,161
Of course I do.

429
00:35:17,161 --> 00:35:20,961
Everyone knows that
Yoon Ha Na is a great actress.

430
00:35:20,961 --> 00:35:24,957
But she's just too obscure. It's a real shame.

431
00:35:26,895 --> 00:35:32,782
Of course, that's why we're working on
slowly but surely making her more famous.

432
00:35:40,208 --> 00:35:41,940
Thank you for coming by. Safe travels.

433
00:35:41,940 --> 00:35:44,008
Let's grab a meal together sometime.

434
00:35:44,008 --> 00:35:45,299
- I'd be honored.
- Nice seeing you.

435
00:35:45,299 --> 00:35:47,405
Have a good day.

436
00:35:48,063 --> 00:35:52,216
Ms. Geum, this is exactly why
I said this won't work.

437
00:35:52,216 --> 00:35:55,654
I need to get my nails done.
What a waste of time.

438
00:35:56,595 --> 00:35:57,866
I don't get it.

439
00:35:57,866 --> 00:35:59,668
Them and their "global" this
and "Korean wave" that.

440
00:35:59,668 --> 00:36:04,039
How are rookies supposed to grow
if all they want are already acclaimed actors?

441
00:36:04,039 --> 00:36:08,168
You'd think those people
were born as global stars.

442
00:36:08,168 --> 00:36:10,234
Whatever, I don't want to work with you.

443
00:36:10,888 --> 00:36:12,259
Just you wait.

444
00:36:12,259 --> 00:36:16,233
Everyone will be lining up
for a chance to cast Ha Na soon enough.

445
00:36:35,735 --> 00:36:36,738
[My Star]

446
00:36:40,181 --> 00:36:43,618
[My Boss]

447
00:36:43,618 --> 00:36:46,395
The person you are calling is unavailable...

448
00:36:46,395 --> 00:36:47,902
[My Star]

449
00:36:55,015 --> 00:36:57,202
[What are you doing tonight? Busy?]
[I'm waiting for the director and writer now]

450
00:37:00,509 --> 00:37:03,093
You're twinkling so bright,

451
00:37:05,502 --> 00:37:08,243
but you're too far away to hold on to.

452
00:37:10,642 --> 00:37:13,820
So who is this Park Gi Tae guy?

453
00:37:25,022 --> 00:37:26,989
[Lee Hyeong Won]

454
00:37:26,989 --> 00:37:30,337
The day I got my first gold medal
as a judo player,

455
00:37:34,122 --> 00:37:37,165
- he said he didn't like seeing me win.
- Let go of me!

456
00:37:39,369 --> 00:37:41,462
He wanted to stop me from playing ever again.

457
00:37:41,462 --> 00:37:43,575
So he slit my wrist.

458
00:37:43,575 --> 00:37:45,275
Evil incarnate.

459
00:38:03,662 --> 00:38:06,987
Do you know where he is now?

460
00:38:08,762 --> 00:38:10,170
No, I don't.

461
00:38:11,569 --> 00:38:13,293
You don't?

462
00:38:13,293 --> 00:38:16,183
He left the orphanage
as soon as he became an adult,

463
00:38:16,183 --> 00:38:19,227
but it's pretty obvious
where troubled kids like him would end up.

464
00:38:23,409 --> 00:38:25,006
Where?

465
00:38:25,006 --> 00:38:28,809
Somewhere you can get paid
to do illegal things.

466
00:38:30,209 --> 00:38:31,909
Which is exactly...

467
00:38:32,555 --> 00:38:34,255
what led him back to me.

468
00:38:45,218 --> 00:38:49,222
We ran the license plate, and sure enough,
the bike was registered as stolen.

469
00:38:49,222 --> 00:38:53,807
We'll secure the security footage
and track him down.

470
00:38:59,423 --> 00:39:01,331
I did some digging
on his peers from the orphanage,

471
00:39:01,331 --> 00:39:04,635
and on illegal motorcycle dealers as well,

472
00:39:04,635 --> 00:39:06,534
but there's no trace of him.

473
00:39:07,123 --> 00:39:08,851
This was a planned disappearance.

474
00:39:08,851 --> 00:39:12,606
Nobody, not even me, will ever find this guy.

475
00:39:16,421 --> 00:39:18,121
[Detective Gonan]
[Simple to hire, results sure as fire!]

476
00:39:20,741 --> 00:39:22,881
He seems like a weirdo.

477
00:39:22,881 --> 00:39:24,198
Really?

478
00:39:24,198 --> 00:39:26,145
But I heard he's really famous.

479
00:39:26,145 --> 00:39:27,551
[Detective Gonan]

480
00:39:34,522 --> 00:39:36,055
[Soo Hyuk]

481
00:39:38,185 --> 00:39:39,482
Yes, Soo Hyuk?

482
00:39:39,482 --> 00:39:41,658
Woo Jae! Where are you?

483
00:39:41,658 --> 00:39:43,724
I just have someone to meet before I go home.

484
00:39:43,724 --> 00:39:46,031
I'll make sure it doesn't interfere
with tomorrow's schedule.

485
00:39:46,031 --> 00:39:47,965
Okay, then.

486
00:39:47,965 --> 00:39:50,035
Good job today.

487
00:39:50,035 --> 00:39:51,735
Thank you.

488
00:40:30,218 --> 00:40:31,666
Woo Jae.

489
00:40:35,325 --> 00:40:37,025
Yes, Director?

490
00:40:37,685 --> 00:40:40,924
Did you know you've never called me "bro?"

491
00:40:42,625 --> 00:40:44,121
I'm...

492
00:40:45,860 --> 00:40:47,724
only staying in my lane.

493
00:40:51,445 --> 00:40:52,988
Woo Jae.

494
00:40:53,611 --> 00:40:55,622
Stay in your lane.

495
00:40:57,916 --> 00:40:59,380
I see.

496
00:41:01,801 --> 00:41:05,045
Stop wasting time and say what you want to say.

497
00:41:05,045 --> 00:41:08,972
What's this about Ha Na quitting acting?

498
00:41:09,608 --> 00:41:12,888
Of course she didn't tell you.

499
00:41:14,621 --> 00:41:16,321
Woo Jae, you...

500
00:41:16,988 --> 00:41:19,639
Do you know anything about Ha Na's camcorder?

501
00:41:34,861 --> 00:41:36,561
What... is this?

502
00:41:39,333 --> 00:41:42,459
Year... 2026?

503
00:41:52,651 --> 00:41:55,645
That's sudden. A camcorder?

504
00:41:56,331 --> 00:41:57,642
What's this about?

505
00:41:58,885 --> 00:42:02,082
In my opinion, Ha Na and her twin brother...

506
00:42:02,082 --> 00:42:03,993
How do I put this...

507
00:42:03,993 --> 00:42:06,065
They seem like different beings.

508
00:42:07,285 --> 00:42:09,155
Didn't you feel it, too?

509
00:42:09,155 --> 00:42:11,583
You're the person closest to them.

510
00:42:13,991 --> 00:42:16,134
I wish you'd start making some sense.

511
00:42:23,265 --> 00:42:26,037
I think the twins came from the future.

512
00:42:27,558 --> 00:42:30,991
Yang Jun Mo is the stalker...

513
00:42:30,991 --> 00:42:33,135
Then what's the deal with Lee Hyeong Won?

514
00:42:33,135 --> 00:42:35,219
What do they have to do with each other?

515
00:42:35,219 --> 00:42:38,777
Besides, didn't he originally disappear
during sophomore year?

516
00:42:38,777 --> 00:42:40,845
What could this mean?

517
00:42:40,845 --> 00:42:43,142
Why would they gang up on not only you,

518
00:42:43,142 --> 00:42:46,243
but Woo Jae as well? There's no reason to!

519
00:42:46,243 --> 00:42:47,967
You know, I...

520
00:42:47,967 --> 00:42:50,930
I hope you live a happy life, Woo Jae.

521
00:42:50,930 --> 00:42:53,473
And a long one at that.

522
00:42:55,337 --> 00:42:58,343
If you're just going to sit there
spouting nonsense,

523
00:42:58,343 --> 00:43:01,402
- I'll see myself out.
- What if it's because of you?

524
00:43:04,983 --> 00:43:07,550
What if the camcorder is a time machine?

525
00:43:08,223 --> 00:43:12,021
What if Ha Na traveled back in time
to save you?

526
00:43:12,021 --> 00:43:14,465
If not, why would she suddenly announce
that she's giving up acting?

527
00:43:14,465 --> 00:43:16,346
It was her lifelong dream.

528
00:43:16,346 --> 00:43:20,126
We don't know what happens in the future.

529
00:43:20,126 --> 00:43:22,197
But one thing's for sure.

530
00:43:22,197 --> 00:43:24,301
You die in the future,

531
00:43:24,301 --> 00:43:29,064
and Ha Na, in an attempt to save you,
ends up giving up on her dream.

532
00:43:36,043 --> 00:43:39,316
Are you sure you're in your right mind?

533
00:43:39,930 --> 00:43:42,510
That just doesn't make any sense...

534
00:43:43,370 --> 00:43:45,083
Do you really think so?

535
00:43:45,083 --> 00:43:47,010
That it doesn't make any sense?

536
00:43:48,870 --> 00:43:50,570
You know, Yoon Ha Ru...

537
00:43:51,190 --> 00:43:55,294
He was a judo prodigy,
but ended up quitting due to an injury, right?

538
00:43:55,294 --> 00:43:57,838
Don't you think that's also because of you?

539
00:43:57,838 --> 00:44:02,035
He traveled back in time to save you
and got his life screwed over.

540
00:44:03,603 --> 00:44:05,073
You!

541
00:44:06,243 --> 00:44:07,943
Stay away!

542
00:44:14,190 --> 00:44:17,654
The twins have thrown everything away
just to save your life,

543
00:44:17,654 --> 00:44:19,225
but you?

544
00:44:19,225 --> 00:44:22,195
Don't you want to protect their lives as well?

545
00:44:22,195 --> 00:44:24,204
What's your point?

546
00:44:27,950 --> 00:44:29,750
The camcorder.

547
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:32,930
They will give everything up for you,
here, in the past.

548
00:44:32,930 --> 00:44:34,802
So we should get rid of it.

549
00:44:37,610 --> 00:44:40,074
It still makes no sense,

550
00:44:40,074 --> 00:44:41,725
but even if it did...

551
00:44:41,725 --> 00:44:44,603
What does this have to do with you?

552
00:44:44,603 --> 00:44:46,527
I want to protect Ha Na's life.

553
00:44:46,527 --> 00:44:49,450
I don't want to lose such a great actress.

554
00:44:49,450 --> 00:44:51,270
Woo Jae, I...

555
00:44:51,270 --> 00:44:54,211
I want Ha Na to live her dream.

556
00:44:55,070 --> 00:44:56,523
Don't you?

557
00:44:57,503 --> 00:44:58,855
You.

558
00:44:59,877 --> 00:45:03,685
Are you sure you can handle watching
their lives fall into misery just for you?

559
00:45:04,430 --> 00:45:06,237
I know you're not.

560
00:45:06,237 --> 00:45:08,937
We may have our differences, you and I,

561
00:45:09,523 --> 00:45:11,468
but we serve the same purpose.

562
00:45:12,477 --> 00:45:14,060
To protect Ha Na.

563
00:45:23,837 --> 00:45:25,961
We may have our differences, you and I,

564
00:45:25,961 --> 00:45:27,525
but we serve the same purpose.

565
00:45:27,525 --> 00:45:29,225
To protect Ha Na.

566
00:45:30,037 --> 00:45:31,963
No!

567
00:45:33,963 --> 00:45:35,647
Woo Jae...

568
00:45:35,647 --> 00:45:37,183
I have to go now.

569
00:45:37,183 --> 00:45:39,574
- To where?
- I don't know.

570
00:45:39,574 --> 00:45:41,487
But when I do...

571
00:45:42,211 --> 00:45:44,610
I might never see you again.

572
00:46:02,137 --> 00:46:03,593
Woo Jae!

573
00:46:09,978 --> 00:46:12,947
Woo Jae. Is there something wrong?

574
00:46:12,947 --> 00:46:14,913
I missed you so much.

575
00:46:16,253 --> 00:46:18,043
You're silly.

576
00:46:18,043 --> 00:46:19,515
Me too.

577
00:47:01,703 --> 00:47:04,054
Jung Woo Jae, you...

578
00:47:04,054 --> 00:47:06,245
feel different today.

579
00:47:23,782 --> 00:47:25,305
I love you.

580
00:47:31,976 --> 00:47:33,571
Me too.

581
00:48:26,251 --> 00:48:28,538
[Happy Home]

582
00:49:01,024 --> 00:49:02,724
Did you sleep well?

583
00:49:05,867 --> 00:49:08,991
What's all this? Jung Woo Jae!

584
00:49:14,288 --> 00:49:16,623
Cute.

585
00:49:16,623 --> 00:49:18,869
Hey, new guy, close your eyes!

586
00:49:20,360 --> 00:49:22,237
- Yes, sir!
- Woo Jae.

587
00:49:22,237 --> 00:49:24,741
This is good. This is all so great,

588
00:49:24,741 --> 00:49:28,139
but I have to remind you once more
that this is Ye Rang Entertainment's quarters.

589
00:49:28,139 --> 00:49:29,676
Yeah, I'm aware.

590
00:49:29,676 --> 00:49:32,173
For your information,
we'll be coming home late today.

591
00:49:32,173 --> 00:49:35,027
And I mean very, very late.

592
00:49:35,027 --> 00:49:36,984
So take that into consideration.

593
00:49:36,984 --> 00:49:39,129
Yeah, me too.

594
00:49:41,786 --> 00:49:43,785
- Let's go.
- Go, go!

595
00:49:44,386 --> 00:49:46,763
- May I open my eyes now?
- Yeah, come on! Let's go.

596
00:49:46,763 --> 00:49:49,413
- Let's go!
- Yes, sir!

597
00:50:16,222 --> 00:50:18,519
What's all this?

598
00:50:33,033 --> 00:50:35,586
I'm sorry you had to see that
first thing in the morning, Seok Min.

599
00:50:35,586 --> 00:50:36,999
No, no.

600
00:50:36,999 --> 00:50:38,939
I didn't see anything!

601
00:50:38,939 --> 00:50:41,028
Hey, Ha Ru?

602
00:50:43,001 --> 00:50:49,314
I've been contemplating
whether I should tell you or not...

603
00:50:49,314 --> 00:50:50,679
What is it?

604
00:51:07,926 --> 00:51:10,898
How did you even come up with all this?

605
00:51:12,239 --> 00:51:14,519
You said you wanted a day to empty your brain

606
00:51:14,519 --> 00:51:17,477
and watch all your favorite movies
until you got sick of them.

607
00:51:17,477 --> 00:51:20,241
That's your idea of a romantic day, right?

608
00:51:23,859 --> 00:51:27,626
No, my idea of a romantic day...

609
00:51:27,626 --> 00:51:29,479
is with you, Jung Woo Jae.

610
00:51:34,906 --> 00:51:36,753
What?

611
00:52:04,799 --> 00:52:06,749
Just until the guys get back home, okay?

612
00:52:09,246 --> 00:52:10,731
Okay.

613
00:52:44,006 --> 00:52:45,397
Woo Jae.

614
00:52:47,346 --> 00:52:50,790
Nothing's wrong, right?

615
00:52:52,719 --> 00:52:54,874
Yeah, nothing's wrong.

616
00:52:56,519 --> 00:52:58,537
If anything goes wrong,

617
00:52:58,537 --> 00:53:00,507
you need to tell me.

618
00:53:00,507 --> 00:53:02,543
You don't have to suffer alone.

619
00:53:05,073 --> 00:53:06,773
Of course.

620
00:53:15,619 --> 00:53:17,015
Ha Na.

621
00:53:17,673 --> 00:53:18,906
Yeah?

622
00:53:21,213 --> 00:53:25,823
Whatever hardships we go through in the future,

623
00:53:27,386 --> 00:53:29,819
we shouldn't give up on our dreams.

624
00:53:29,819 --> 00:53:31,418
Never.

625
00:53:36,493 --> 00:53:39,238
Why are you bringing up dreams all of a sudden?

626
00:53:41,419 --> 00:53:45,057
Aren't you going to answer me?

627
00:53:48,913 --> 00:53:50,230
Of course.

628
00:53:50,230 --> 00:53:51,721
I won't give up.

629
00:53:51,721 --> 00:53:54,404
So you promise?

630
00:53:56,073 --> 00:53:57,773
Promise?

631
00:54:22,526 --> 00:54:24,070
Welcome, table for how many, sir?

632
00:54:24,070 --> 00:54:25,770
I'm here alone.

633
00:54:33,193 --> 00:54:35,906
Do you like watching movies?

634
00:54:35,906 --> 00:54:37,843
I do like movies.

635
00:54:37,843 --> 00:54:39,514
Here's the menu.

636
00:54:39,514 --> 00:54:41,179
Take your time browsing through it.

637
00:54:41,179 --> 00:54:42,282
Hey, actually...

638
00:54:42,282 --> 00:54:45,054
Can I get an iced chocolate, extra sweet?

639
00:54:45,054 --> 00:54:47,685
Okay, I'll take the menu away for you.

640
00:54:47,685 --> 00:54:50,147
I'd like to browse some more.

641
00:54:50,966 --> 00:54:52,666
Right, of course.

642
00:54:58,173 --> 00:55:02,719
I started out as an entry-level employee,
but climbed the ranks faster than the others.

643
00:55:02,719 --> 00:55:05,091
Well, yes, it is my father's company,

644
00:55:05,091 --> 00:55:08,449
but I lived a hardworking life,
and started at the bottom.

645
00:55:08,449 --> 00:55:12,014
I was working while others fooled around.

646
00:55:13,147 --> 00:55:14,564
I see.

647
00:55:20,526 --> 00:55:23,510
You know, we're four years apart.

648
00:55:23,510 --> 00:55:25,959
They say it's the perfect age gap.

649
00:55:25,959 --> 00:55:28,317
What a boring pickup line.

650
00:55:29,186 --> 00:55:30,886
Is that so?

651
00:55:32,291 --> 00:55:33,854
I want to marry fast.

652
00:55:33,854 --> 00:55:37,841
I want to provide my wife with stability.

653
00:55:37,841 --> 00:55:40,330
The outside world is like a war zone.

654
00:55:40,330 --> 00:55:43,559
I don't want my beloved to struggle alone.

655
00:55:43,559 --> 00:55:48,003
I want to let her rest easy
behind the fence that I built.

656
00:55:51,106 --> 00:55:53,265
That's a beautiful sentiment.

657
00:55:55,355 --> 00:55:57,311
"A beautiful sentiment?"

658
00:57:28,986 --> 00:57:30,810
Ms. Ye Rang.

659
00:57:30,810 --> 00:57:32,134
Yes?

660
00:57:32,134 --> 00:57:34,158
Please think fondly of me.

661
00:57:34,158 --> 00:57:36,746
- Pardon me?
- Love at first sight...

662
00:57:36,746 --> 00:57:38,323
I never believed in it,

663
00:57:38,323 --> 00:57:41,547
but having met you today, I do now.

664
00:57:41,547 --> 00:57:45,765
I think I'm only going to fall deeper for you.

665
00:58:15,093 --> 00:58:16,793
Woo Jae.

666
00:58:29,593 --> 00:58:31,293
That bastard!

667
00:59:21,493 --> 00:59:23,536
What are you doing, Woo Jae?

668
00:59:29,466 --> 00:59:31,423
Are you alright, sir?

669
00:59:33,240 --> 00:59:34,623
Sir?

670
00:59:43,413 --> 00:59:45,523
- Who, me?
- Yes.

671
00:59:46,693 --> 00:59:48,680
I'm absolutely fine.

672
00:59:49,631 --> 00:59:51,842
Call me if you need anything.

673
00:59:51,842 --> 00:59:53,093
Okay.

674
01:00:25,197 --> 01:00:27,721
Why is this here?

675
01:00:32,150 --> 01:00:33,368
Sorry.

676
01:00:33,368 --> 01:00:36,655
I dropped it. I think it broke.

677
01:00:38,537 --> 01:00:41,908
It's okay. It's always been a piece of junk.

678
01:00:41,908 --> 01:00:44,513
It held up for longer than I thought it would.

679
01:01:29,982 --> 01:01:32,848
The contents of the script... changed.

680
01:01:32,848 --> 01:01:35,571
If I can't have you for myself...

681
01:01:35,571 --> 01:01:37,173
The camcorder...

682
01:01:37,173 --> 01:01:39,009
It's gone!

683
01:01:39,009 --> 01:01:41,322
Every action we take

684
01:01:41,322 --> 01:01:43,036
can't be reversed anymore.

685
01:01:43,036 --> 01:01:45,386
Unless you want to ruin what we have left,

686
01:01:45,386 --> 01:01:47,990
at least have some respect.

687
01:01:47,990 --> 01:01:50,961
The reason why you're traveling through time
is to save my life,

688
01:01:50,961 --> 01:01:52,685
is that right?

689
01:01:52,685 --> 01:01:54,381
Please, just stop.

690
01:01:54,381 --> 01:01:56,925
The true finale...

691
01:01:56,925 --> 01:01:59,051
is only starting now.
